## Nothing is currently bundled

As of this revision, Airlock **bundles and redistributes no third-party
component**. It has no runtime dependency beyond a C11 compiler, a POSIX libc,
and (optionally) ALSA for desktop audio output, all of which are linked against
the host system rather than shipped by us.

That is a deliberate property and it is enforced by review: the table below
lists components Airlock is *designed to invoke on the host or to fetch with the
user's explicit consent* — it does not mean they are in the repository.

## Components Airlock invokes or may fetch

Airlock is an orchestrator. Its job is to locate, configure, and launch mature
upstream components as **separate processes**, not to reimplement them. When a
component is merely executed as a separate program that the user installed or
explicitly consented to download, Airlock does not create a derivative work of
it and does not redistribute it.

| Component | Role in Airlock | Upstream license | Bundled today? | Redistribution obligation if bundled |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| [Wine](https://www.winehq.org/) | Compatibility Mode runtime | LGPL-2.1-or-later | No | Ship the full license text, state changes, and provide corresponding source. Do not statically link Airlock's MIT code into it. |
| [Box86](https://github.com/ptitSeb/box86) | x86 user-mode translation on ARM | MIT | No | Preserve copyright notice and permission notice. |
| [Box64](https://github.com/ptitSeb/box64) | x86_64 user-mode translation on ARM | MIT | No | Preserve copyright notice and permission notice. |
| [DXVK](https://github.com/doitsujin/dxvk) | Direct3D 9/10/11 → Vulkan | Zlib | No | Preserve copyright notice and permission notice. |
| [VKD3D-Proton](https://github.com/HansKristian-Work/vkd3d-proton) | Direct3D 12 → Vulkan | LGPL-2.1 | No | Ship the full license text, state changes, and provide corresponding source. |
| [QEMU](https://www.qemu.org/) | VM Mode full-system virtualizer | GPL-2.0-only (some parts BSD/MIT — verify per revision) | No | GPL-2.0 applies to the distributed QEMU binary and requires corresponding source. **Airlock's own code must stay a separate program invoking QEMU through `execve`; do not link against QEMU internals.** |
| [Mesa](https://www.mesa3d.org/) | Host Vulkan/OpenGL drivers | MIT (plus Khronos/SGI/Boost parts) | No | Preserve copyright notices. |
| ALSA (`libasound`) | Desktop audio output | LGPL-2.1 | No (system library, optional build flag) | Dynamic linking against a system library imposes no redistribution duty on us. |

License facts above were checked against upstream project documentation on
2026-08-30. **Re-verify against the exact revision before any component is
bundled** — licenses and dual-licensing terms change.

## Rules for adding a bundled component

A component may only be added to a release when all of the following exist:

1. An entry in this file naming the component, its **exact upstream revision or
   version**, its license, and the obligations that apply.
2. The complete license text under `licenses/<component>/`.
3. A reproducible build script under `third_party/<component>/` that fetches
   that exact revision and builds it.
4. One patch per local modification under `patches/<component>/`, each with a
   header stating why it exists and whether it has been sent upstream.
5. An entry in the in-app licenses screen.
6. Confirmation that the license permits redistribution in the form we ship
   (source, binary, or both). If it does not, the component is fetched at
   runtime with the user's explicit consent instead of being bundled.

## Components we will not bundle

- Microsoft Windows in any form: system files, DLLs, drivers, installation
  media, product keys, activation tooling, or branding. VM Mode requires the
  user to supply their own legally obtained ISO and license.
- Copyrighted fonts, codecs, or game data.
- Anti-cheat, DRM-circumvention, or malware-evasion components.

